          "FORMAL RESTATEMENT": "Definitions/Conventions.\n- For $N\\ge 1$, write $A(N):=|A\\cap\\{1,\\dots,N\\}|$.\n- ``Triple sums are all distinct aside from trivial coincidences'' is interpreted as the $B_3$ condition:\n  for any $a_1\\le a_2\\le a_3$ and $b_1\\le b_2\\le b_3$ in $A$,\n  \\[a_1+a_2+a_3=b_1+b_2+b_3 \\implies (a_1,a_2,a_3)=(b_1,b_2,b_3).\\]\n  Equivalently, the multiset $\\{a,b,c\\}$ is uniquely determined by its sum $a+b+c$.\n\nQuestion.\nIf $A\\subset\\mathbb N$ is infinite and satisfies the above $B_3$ condition, must one have\n\\[\\liminf_{N\\to\\infty} \\frac{A(N)}{N^{1/3}}=0?\\]",
